! Antclock Engine

Full implementation of CE2 antclock concepts for JavaScript/TiddlyWiki.

!! Core Concepts

=== Experiential Time ===

Time measured by meaningful state changes, not clock ticks:

```javascript
var engine = require("$:/core/modules/utils/antclock-engine.js").default;
engine.tickExperiential("ready"); // Increments experiential time
console.log(engine.experientialTime); // Number of state transitions
```

=== Self-Timing ===

Recursive self-checking with exponential backoff:

```javascript
engine.selfTime(
	function() {
		return someCondition() ? "ready" : "pending";
	},
	function(state, attempts, expTime) {
		// Ready! attempts = number of checks, expTime = experiential time
	}
);
```

=== Self-Visibility ===

Observe state changes:

```javascript
var unsubscribe = engine.observe(function(newState, oldState, expTime) {
	console.log("State changed:", oldState, "->", newState, "at", expTime);
});
// Later: unsubscribe();
```

=== Grammar Adjusting ===

Self-correcting error handling:

```javascript
// Automatically handles errors and recovers
engine.selfTime(checkCondition, onReady);
// Errors are logged and system adapts
```

=== Phase Resonance ===

Synchronize timing with system phases:

```javascript
engine.setPhaseResonance(0.5); // 0-1 strength
// Timing adjusts based on system phase
```

=== Guardian Boundaries ===

Semantic boundaries that protect system integrity:

```javascript
engine.addGuardian("wiki-available", function() {
	return $tw && $tw.wiki !== undefined;
});

var violations = engine.checkGuardians();
if(violations.length > 0) {
	console.log("Guardian violations:", violations);
}
```

!! Usage Examples

=== Wait for Macro ===

```javascript
var engine = require("$:/core/modules/utils/antclock-engine.js").default;

engine.waitForMacro("$my-widget", function() {
	console.log("Widget ready!");
});
```

=== Reactive Wait ===

```javascript
engine.reactiveWait(
	function() {
		return condition() ? "ready" : "pending";
	},
	function() {
		// Ready - combines self-timing + event listening
	}
);
```

=== Custom Engine Instance ===

```javascript
var AntclockEngine = require("$:/core/modules/utils/antclock-engine.js").AntclockEngine;
var myEngine = new AntclockEngine({
	name: "my-engine",
	maxAttempts: 30,
	baseDelay: 100
});

myEngine.selfTime(checkCondition, onReady);
```

=== Engine Statistics ===

```javascript
var stats = engine.getStats();
console.log(stats);
// {
//   experientialTime: 15,
//   currentState: "ready",
//   grammarAdjustments: 2,
//   activeTimers: 1,
//   observers: 3,
//   guardians: 2,
//   phase: 1.2,
//   phaseResonance: 0.5
// }
```

!! Benefits Over Simple Utilities

* **Experiential Time Tracking** - Know how many meaningful changes occurred
* **Self-Visibility** - Observe your own state transitions
* **Grammar Adjusting** - Automatic error recovery and adaptation
* **Phase Resonance** - Synchronize with system rhythms
* **Guardian Boundaries** - Protect system integrity
* **Statistics** - Monitor engine health and performance

!! Integration with TiddlyWiki

The engine automatically integrates with TiddlyWiki's event system and provides grammar-adjusting error handling that works seamlessly with TiddlyWiki's architecture.

